        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c209968e-847b-50dc-9d9b-420a62d09508",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Species: Elachista canapennella\n- Places: Fennoscandia, northern Russia, the Pyrenees, Italy, Romania, Ireland, central Russia, Finland, Scandinavia\n- Concepts: Elachistidae, Fennoscandian, Spitz-type dogs\n- Animals: Elkhounds\n- People: Leo Palin\n- Roles: retired professional tennis player\n\nFacts:\n- Elachista canapennella is a moth in the family Elachistidae.\n- Elachista canapennella is found from Fennoscandia and northern Russia to the Pyrenees, Italy, and Romania, and from Ireland to central Russia.\n- The name Fennoscandia comes from the Latin words \"Fennia\" for Finland and \"Scandia\" for Scandinavian.\n- Elkhounds are a group of Fennoscandian dog breeds that belong to the Spitz-type dogs and are used for hunting elk or moose and other large animals.\n- Leo Palin was born on 20 October 1956 and is a retired professional tennis player from Finland.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "68e1f5b5-4f28-57fc-9b3d-63c499f810c5",
        "text": "Page: Elachista canapennella. Sentence: Elachista canapennella is a moth of the Elachistidae family.\nPage: Elachista canapennella. Sentence: It is found from Fennoscandia and northern Russia to the Pyrenees, Italy and Romania and from Ireland to central Russia.\nPage: Fennoscandia. Sentence: Its name comes from the Latin words \"Fennia\" (Finland) and \"Scandia\" (Scandinavian).\nPage: Elkhound. Sentence: Elkhounds are a group of Fennoscandian dog breeds belonging to the Spitz-type dogs and used for hunting elk/moose and other large animals.\nPage: Leo Palin. Sentence: Leo Palin (born 20 October 1956) is a retired professional tennis player from Finland.",
